 ## Definition
 
-Fix a material constitution $c$ and its equilibrium state domain $D_c$ from [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]]. Use the protocol functional $Q:\mathcal P_s\to\mathbb R$ (values in joules) supplied by [[def-td-process-and-protocol]] on all admitted records; its existence on this full class does not extend the core-only energy-balance law. For $x,y\in D_c$, write $x\prec_c y$, and say that $y$ is adiabatically accessible from $x$, exactly when the declared process model admits at least one record $P\in\mathcal P_s$ from [[def-td-process-and-protocol]] with $x_P^-=x$, $x_P^+=y$, $Q[P]=0$, and the model’s stated auxiliary and work-device endpoint conditions satisfied. The material constitution is the same at both endpoints. The process record must account for the selected outer boundary and every auxiliary included by its protocol.
+Fix a material constitution $c$ and its equilibrium state domain $D_c$ from [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]]. Use the protocol functional $Q:\mathcal P_s\to\mathbb R$ (values in joules) supplied by [[def-td-process-and-protocol]] on all admitted records; its existence on this full class does not extend the core-only energy-balance law. For $x,y\in D_c$, write $x\prec_c y$, and say that $y$ is adiabatically accessible from $x$, exactly when the declared process model admits at least one record $P\in\mathcal P_s$ from [[def-td-process-and-protocol]] with $x_P^-=x$, $x_P^+=y$, $a_s(P)=1$ (hence $Q[P]=0$), and the model’s stated auxiliary and work-device endpoint conditions satisfied. The material constitution is the same at both endpoints. The process record must account for the selected outer boundary and every auxiliary included by its protocol.
 
-The sign convention is $Q>0$ into the system and $W_{\mathrm{on}}>0$ for work done on it, as fixed in [[def-td-process-and-protocol]]. Thus adiabatic means zero protocol-assigned heat, not zero work, zero energy change, isolation, quasistatic evolution, or reversibility. The relation concerns equilibrium endpoints only; intermediate configurations may be nonequilibrium. Existence of a witness record is model input, not a consequence of this definition.
+The sign convention is $Q>0$ into the system and $W_{\mathrm{on}}>0$ for work done on it, as fixed in [[def-td-process-and-protocol]]. Thus adiabatic means no thermal transfer across the selected outer boundary throughout the record, as specified by the supplier’s predicate; zero net heat alone is insufficient. It does not require zero work, zero energy change, isolation, quasistatic evolution, or reversibility. The relation concerns equilibrium endpoints only; intermediate configurations may be nonequilibrium. Existence of a witness record is model input, not a consequence of this definition.
 
 When the constitution is clear, write $x\prec y$. Define $x\sim y$ by $x\prec y$ and $y\prec x$, and $x\prec\prec y$ by $x\prec y$ and not $y\prec x$. These are respectively accessibility equivalence and strict one-way accessibility; neither is defined by equality of energy alone.
 
